# Everything in .forge/ is committed — the registry, the baselines and the vendored
# checkers. A fresh clone must be held to the same rules as this one, so nothing here
# is machine-local by default, and this file is the only place an exception may be
# declared.
#
# A trailing comment on a pattern line becomes part of the pattern, so each
# exception gets its own line above it.

# A stale cache of forge_knowledge; the MCP server is the source of truth
# (see CLAUDE.local.md — there is no local knowledge file by design).
knowledge.json

# Anything a tool writes per machine.
*.local.*

# The Forge orientation names one Forge instance's project (its id and slug), and this
# repository is worked from two: beta and dev. A committed one sent every dev checkout
# to beta's project id, which dev core answers 404 for. The runner writes each
# checkout's own into CLAUDE.local.md on provision and every refresh
# (packages/runner/crates/runner-workspace/src/orientation.rs).
orientation.md
